# src/cli follow-ups

- `version.rs::require_validate_pass` leaves an untracked `.mars/` directory after its
  dry-run. Make validation avoid creating canonical state or remove only the state that
  this invocation created, so an aborted release can be rerun from a clean tree.
- `provide.rs`: a provided bundle is host-authored v1 and read strictly (pre-v1 translation
  covers only dependency trees), so one removed key in one skill refuses the whole bundle
  with exit 2. meridian-cli falls back to its wheel skills on exit 2 without printing
  Mars's error, so a later Mars that removes a key would silently downgrade an older
  Meridian. Either refuse per skill, or have meridian-cli print the
  `provided-skill-invalid` message.
